 "info": {
  "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official Amazon EC2 Container Service API (2014-11-13). Every other official operation returns HTTP 501 UnknownOperationException. Clusters and task definitions are configuration metadata: no container instance, task, service, task set or Fargate capacity is started, so cluster counts stay 0. RunTask, StartTask, CreateService and other workload APIs return UnknownOperationException with HTTP 501. Clusters accept only the AWS-managed FARGATE and FARGATE_SPOT capacity providers; Service Connect namespaces do not exist. A missing clusterName creates the default cluster and DescribeClusters without clusters describes it. Creating a live cluster name again is refused. DescribeClusters and DescribeTaskDefinition always return settings, configuration and tags, and failures name the identifier as supplied. Each task definition family holds one revision (1): registering a live family again is refused and other revisions do not exist. Deregistration deletes the revision after returning it INACTIVE. Fargate task definitions must use awsvpc networking and a documented Linux task CPU and memory combination. familyPrefix and sort are refused.",
  "title": "Amazon Elastic Container Service (simulator catalog)",
  "version": "2014-11-13"
 },
